INTENDED USE
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

This software is provided for RESEARCH AND EDUCATIONAL USE ONLY.

It is not a medical device. It is not FDA-cleared, CE-marked, or approved by any
regulatory authority, and it has not been validated for diagnosis, treatment,
monitoring, or any clinical decision.

Outputs named after clinical rating scales (including but not limited to UPDRS,
MoCA, Berg Balance Scale, Tinetti, Hoehn-Yahr, TUG and PDQ-39) are model
estimates produced by this software. They are NOT clinical scores, are not
equivalent to an administered assessment, and must not be interpreted or
reported as such.

Any percentile, z-score, impairment classification, or change score computed by
this software against its bundled reference values is a demonstration of the
arithmetic only. The bundled reference values are illustrative placeholders
(see below) and support no clinical or psychometric conclusion.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
ILLUSTRATIVE REFERENCE VALUES
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The reference values distributed in the `dpb-norms` crate are ILLUSTRATIVE
PLACEHOLDERS that exist to demonstrate and exercise the normative-comparison
API. They are not drawn from any published cohort and they carry no citations.
They must not be used to interpret a measurement from a real person.

Reliability coefficients used to derive SEM, MDC and RCI are likewise
illustrative defaults, not measured test-retest coefficients. The SEM/MDC/RCI
formulas themselves are standard and correct; only the constants supplied to
them are placeholders.

Users intending to draw research conclusions must supply their own reference
values from cited sources and report those citations.

